# Free, auto-refreshing list of US-listed companies

This repository builds and automatically refreshes a CSV of US-exchange-listed operating companies.

The dataset combines Nasdaq Trader security listings with SEC EDGAR company information.

The workflow runs automatically every Monday through GitHub Actions.

## Files

- `fetch_us_stock_universe.py` — builds the company dataset
- `.github/workflows/refresh-stock-list.yml` — automatically refreshes the dataset
- `us_listed_companies.csv` — generated company list
- `us_listed_companies.xlsx` — generated Excel version

## Data sources

### Nasdaq Trader

Used for:

- ticker symbol
- exchange
- security name
- ETF flag
- test-issue flag

### SEC EDGAR

Used for:

- company name
- CIK
- SIC code
- SIC industry description
- state of incorporation
- fiscal year end
- SEC-listed exchange information
- former company names
- public/listing date when explicitly identifiable in SEC registration filings

No Alpha Vantage or other commercial market-data service is required.

## SEC Public Date

The `SEC Public Date` field is intentionally conservative.

The SEC does not provide a universal structured `IPO Date` field for every company.

Therefore this project does **not** infer a public date from:

- the first SEC filing date
- the first 10-K
- the first 10-Q
- the incorporation date
- the first appearance of the ticker
- the registration filing date
- the date a registration became effective by itself

Instead, the script searches appropriate SEC registration filings, including forms such as:

- S-1
- S-1/A
- F-1
- F-1/A
- SB-1
- SB-1/A
- SB-2
- SB-2/A

The script looks for explicit language indicating that the company or its shares became publicly traded or that the initial public offering occurred on a particular date.

If the SEC filing data does not provide a sufficiently explicit date, `SEC Public Date` is left blank.

This is deliberate: a blank value is preferable to an inferred or potentially incorrect IPO date.

## Output columns

| Column | Source |
|---|---|
| Ticker | Nasdaq Trader |
| Company Name | SEC, falling back to Nasdaq |
| Exchange | Nasdaq Trader |
| Industry (SIC Description) | SEC |
| SIC Code | SEC |
| CIK | SEC |
| State of Incorporation | SEC |
| Fiscal Year End | SEC |
| SEC Public Date | SEC registration filings, when explicitly available |
| Former Name(s) | SEC |
| SEC Exchange(s) | SEC |

## SEC User-Agent

The SEC expects automated requests to identify the application/user.

Create this GitHub repository secret:

```text
SEC_USER_AGENT
